{
  "summary": "This experiment established the performance floor for the image modality using a single-profile, image-only configuration with a ResNet-50 encoder (no RNA, no aggregation, no fusion), achieving a validation accuracy of 0.208 and F1 of 0.172. This is substantially below the RNA-only baselines (0.485 for PCA-2000, 0.520 for scvi_n200), suggesting that image features carry very weak independent predictive signal for this classification task. It remains uncertain whether image features could still contribute meaningfully when fused with RNA representations, whether alternative image encoders or preprocessing might recover more signal, or whether the low performance reflects a fundamental limitation of the image modality for this task."
}

